T257	Cue 29679 29683	said
T258	Quotation 29735 30070	"It is an ordinary plumber's smoke- rocket, fitted with a cap at either end to make it self-lighting. Your task is confined to that. When you raise your cry of fire, it will be taken up by quite a number of people. You may then walk to the end of the street, and I will rejoin you in ten minutes. I hope that I have made myself clear?"
T259	Quotation 30071 30253	"I am to remain neutral, to get near the window, to watch you, and at the signal to throw in this object, then to raise the cry of fire, and to wait you at the corner of the street."
T260	Quotation 30254 30266	"Precisely."
T261	Quotation 30303 30407	"That is excellent. I think, perhaps, it is almost time that I prepare for the new role I have to play."
T262	Quotation 30267 30302	"Then you may entirely rely on me."
T263	Quotation 31773 31783	"You see,"
T264	Cue 31784 31792	remarked
T265	Entity 31793 31799	Holmes
T266	Quotation 31847 32142	"this marriage rather simplifies matters. The photograph becomes a double-edged weapon now. The chances are that she would be as averse to its being seen by Mr. Godfrey Norton, as our client is to its coming to the eyes of his princess. Now the question is, Where are we to find the photograph?"
T267	Quotation 32143 32159	"Where, indeed?"
T268	Quotation 32160 32476	"It is most unlikely that she carries it about with her. It is cabinet size. Too large for easy concealment about a woman's dress. She knows that the King is capable of having her waylaid and searched. Two attempts of the sort have already been made. We may take it, then, that she does not carry it about with her."
T269	Quotation 32477 32491	"Where, then?"
T270	Quotation 32492 32995	"Her banker or her lawyer. There is that double possibility. But I am inclined to think neither. Women are naturally secretive, and they like to do their own secreting. Why should she hand it over to anyone else? She could trust her own guardianship, but she could not tell what indirect or political influence might be brought to bear upon a business man. Besides, remember that she had resolved to use it within a few days. It must be where she can lay her hands upon it. It must be in her own house."
T271	Quotation 32996 33028	"But it has twice been burgled."
T272	Quotation 33029 33068	"Pshaw! They did not know how to look."
T273	Quotation 33069 33093	"But how will you look?"
T274	Quotation 33094 33112	"I will not look."
T275	Quotation 33113 33125	"What then?"
T276	Quotation 33126 33154	"I will get her to show me."
T277	Quotation 33155 33177	"But she will refuse."
T278	Quotation 33178 33296	"She will not be able to. But I hear the rumble of wheels. It is her carriage. Now carry out my orders to the letter."
T279	Quotation 34653 34687	"Is the poor gentleman much hurt?"
T280	Entity 34688 34691	she
T281	Cue 34692 34697	asked
T282	Quotation 34699 34712	"He is dead,"
T283	Quotation 34735 34765	"No, no, there's life in him!"
T284	Cue 34713 34718	cried
T285	Entity 34719 34733	several voices
T286	Cue 34766 34773	shouted
T287	Entity 34774 34781	another
T288	Quotation 34783 34838	"But he'll be gone before you can get him to hospital."
T289	Quotation 34839 34861	"He's a brave fellow,"
T290	Cue 34862 34866	said
T291	Entity 34867 34874	a woman
T292	Quotation 34876 35015	"They would have had the lady's purse and watch if it hadn't been for him. They were a gang, and a rough one, too. Ah, he's breathing now."
T293	Quotation 35016 35072	"He can't lie in the street. May we bring him in, marm?"
T294	Quotation 35073 35162	"Surely. Bring him into the sitting-room. There is a comfortable sofa. This way, please!"
T295	Quotation 36266 36273	"Fire!"
T296	Cue 36257 36265	a cry of
T297	Entity 36219 36220	I
T298	Quotation 36983 37016	"You did it very nicely, Doctor,"
T299	Entity 37017 37019	he
T300	Cue 37020 37028	remarked
T301	Quotation 37030 37080	"Nothing could have been better. It is all right."
T302	Quotation 37081 37107	"You have the photograph?"
T303	Quotation 37108 37129	"I know where it is."
T304	Quotation 37130 37157	"And how did you find out?"
T305	Quotation 37158 37199	"She showed me, as I told you she would."
T306	Quotation 37200 37225	"I am still in the dark."
T307	Quotation 37226 37260	"I do not wish to make a mystery,"
T308	Cue 37261 37265	said
T309	Entity 37266 37268	he
T310	Quotation 37280 37420	"The matter was perfectly simple. You, of course, saw that everyone in the street was an accomplice. They were all engaged for the evening."
T311	Quotation 37421 37441	"I guessed as much."
T312	Quotation 37442 37637	"Then, when the row broke out, I had a little moist red paint in the palm of my hand. I rushed forward, fell down, clapped my hand to my face, and became a piteous spectacle. It is an old trick."
T313	Quotation 37638 37665	"That also I could fathom."
T314	Quotation 37666 37997	"Then they carried me in. She was bound to have me in. What else could she do? And into her sitting-room, which was the very room which I suspected. It lay between that and her bedroom, and I was determined to see which. They laid me on a couch, I motioned for air, they were compelled to open the window, and you had your chance."
T315	Quotation 37998 38022	"How did that help you?"
T316	Quotation 38023 39279	"It was all-important. When a woman thinks that her house is on fire, her instinct is at once to rush to the thing which she values most. It is a perfectly overpowering impulse, and I have more than once taken advantage of it. In the case of the Darlington substitution scandal it was of use to me, and also in the Arnsworth Castle business. A married woman grabs at her baby; an unmarried one reaches for her jewel-box. Now it was clear to me that our lady of to-day had nothing in the house more precious to her than what we are in quest of. She would rush to secure it. The alarm of fire was admirably done. The smoke and shouting were enough to shake nerves of steel. She responded beautifully. The photograph is in a recess behind a sliding panel just above the right bell-pull. She was there in an instant, and I caught a glimpse of it as she half-drew it out. When I cried out that it was a false alarm, she replaced it, glanced at the rocket, rushed from the room, and I have not seen her since. I rose, and, making my excuses, escaped from the house. I hesitated whether to attempt to secure the photograph at once; but the coachman had come in, and as he was watching me narrowly it seemed safer to wait. A little over-precipitance may ruin all."
T317	Quotation 39280 39290	"And now?"
T318	Entity 39291 39292	I
T319	Cue 39293 39298	asked
T320	Quotation 39300 39636	"Our quest is practically finished. I shall call with the King to-morrow, and with you, if you care to come with us. We will be shown into the sitting-room to wait for the lady, but it is probable that when she comes she may find neither us nor the photograph. It might be a satisfaction to his Majesty to regain it with his own hands."
T321	Quotation 39637 39662	"And when will you call?"
T322	Quotation 39663 39882	"At eight in the morning. She will not be up, so that we shall have a clear field. Besides, we must be prompt, for this marriage may mean a complete change in her life and habits. I must wire to the King without delay."
T323	Entity 39986 40001	someone passing
T324	Cue 40002 40006	said
T325	Quotation 40008 40045	"Good-night, Mister Sherlock Holmes."
T326	Quotation 40186 40217	"I've heard that voice before,"
T327	Cue 40218 40222	said
T328	Entity 40223 40229	Holmes
T329	Quotation 40266 40317	"Now, I wonder who the deuce that could have been."
T330	Quotation 40467 40492	"You have really got it!"
T331	Entity 40493 40495	he
T332	Cue 40496 40501	cried
T333	Entity 40512 40527	Sherlock Holmes
T334	Quotation 40582 40592	"Not yet."
T335	Quotation 40593 40614	"But you have hopes?"
T336	Quotation 40615 40630	"I have hopes."
T337	Quotation 40631 40676	"Then, come. I am all impatience to be gone."
T338	Quotation 40677 40698	"We must have a cab."
T339	Quotation 40699 40728	"No, my brougham is waiting."
T340	Quotation 40729 40763	"Then that will simplify matters."
T341	Quotation 40821 40846	"Irene Adler is married,"
T342	Cue 40847 40855	remarked
T343	Entity 40856 40862	Holmes
T344	Quotation 40864 40880	"Married! When?"
T345	Quotation 40881 40893	"Yesterday."
T346	Quotation 40894 40908	"But to whom?"
T347	Quotation 40909 40945	"To an English lawyer named Norton."
T348	Quotation 40946 40975	"But she could not love him."
T349	Quotation 40976 41006	"I am in hopes that she does."
T350	Quotation 41007 41026	"And why in hopes?"
T351	Quotation 41027 41262	"Because it would spare your Majesty all fear of future annoyance. If the lady loves her husband, she does not love your Majesty. If she does not love your Majesty, there is no reason why she should interfere with your Majesty's plan."
T352	Quotation 41263 41365	"It is true. And yet-- Well! I wish she had been of my own station! What a queen she would have made!"
T354	Quotation 41606 41639	"Mr. Sherlock Holmes, I believe?"
T355	Cue 41640 41644	said
T356	Entity 41645 41648	she
T357	Quotation 41752 41906	"Indeed! My mistress told me that you were likely to call. She left this morning with her husband by the 5:15 train from Charing Cross for the Continent."
T358	Cue 41669 41677	answered
T359	Entity 41678 41690	my companion
T360	Quotation 41650 41668	"I am Mr. Holmes,"
T361	Quotation 41907 41914	"What!"
T362	Entity 41915 41930	Sherlock Holmes
T363	Quotation 41980 42020	"Do you mean that she has left England?"
T364	Quotation 42021 42039	"Never to return."
T365	Quotation 42040 42057	"And the papers?"
T366	Cue 42058 42063	asked
T367	Entity 42064 42072	the King
T368	Quotation 42083 42097	"All is lost."
T369	Quotation 42098 42113	"We shall see."
T370	Quotation 44419 44453	"What a woman-- oh, what a woman!"
T371	Cue 44454 44459	cried
T372	Entity 44460 44479	the King of Bohemia
T373	Quotation 44522 44665	"Did I not tell you how quick and resolute she was? Would she not have made an admirable queen? Is it not a pity that she was not on my level?"
T374	Quotation 44666 44767	"From what I have seen of the lady she seems indeed to be on a very different level to your Majesty,"
T375	Cue 44768 44772	said
T376	Entity 44773 44779	Holmes
T377	Quotation 44788 44892	"I am sorry that I have not been able to bring your Majesty's business to a more successful conclusion."
T378	Quotation 44893 44924	"On the contrary, my dear sir,"
T379	Cue 44925 44930	cried
T380	Entity 44931 44939	the King
T381	Quotation 44941 45068	"nothing could be more successful. I know that her word is inviolate. The photograph is now as safe as if it were in the fire."
T382	Quotation 45069 45109	"I am glad to hear your Majesty say so."
T383	Quotation 45110 45200	"I am immensely indebted to you. Pray tell me in what way I can reward you. This ring -- "
T384	Entity 45201 45203	He
T385	Quotation 45293 45360	"Your Majesty has something which I should value even more highly,"
T386	Cue 45361 45365	said
T387	Entity 45366 45372	Holmes
T388	Quotation 45374 45400	"You have but to name it."
T389	Quotation 45401 45419	"This photograph!"
T390	Quotation 45457 45478	"Irene's photograph!"
T391	Entity 45479 45481	he
T392	Cue 45482 45487	cried
T393	Quotation 45489 45517	"Certainly, if you wish it."
T394	Quotation 45518 45640	"I thank your Majesty. Then there is no more to be done in the matter. I have the honour to wish you a very good-morning."
